  "summary": "The code contains a critical security vulnerability due to the use of pickle for deserialization, alongside missing input validation and poor maintainability. The refactored code replaces pickle with JSON, adds input size limits, and includes robust error handling to prevent crashes and exploitation.",
  "fixed_code": "import base64\nimport json\nfrom flask import Flask, request, abort\n\napp = Flask(__name__)\n\nMAX_DATA_SIZE = 1024 * 10  # 10KB limit\n\n@app.route(\"/profile\")\ndef deserialize_data() -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Get base64 encoded JSON data from request, validate size, \n    and return the decoded object.\n    \"\"\"\n    raw_data = request.args.get(\"data\")\n    if not raw_data:\n        abort(400, description=\"Missing data parameter\")\n    \n    if len(raw_data) > MAX_DATA_SIZE:\n        abort(413, description=\"Data too large\")\n\n    try:\n        decoded_bytes = base64.b64decode(raw_data)\n        obj = json.loads(decoded_bytes)\n        return str(obj)\n    except (ValueError, json.JSONDecodeError, TypeError):\n        abort(400, description=\"Invalid data format\")"
